46
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,840
Press and fold to make the fold width larger.

47
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,840
If the fold size is not large, it is necessary to fold it.

48
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,840
If the fold is small, it will not be comfortable.

49
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,840
It's a little difficult to lower the fold length to the shoulder.

50
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:04,840
In this way, there will be a difference in length between the front and back pieces, and there will be some small wrinkles in the front piece.

51
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:12,840
Then you can apply the ratio of 99 to the side.

52
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:24,840
There will be some wrinkles. This method is also suitable for the side of the sleeve and the side of the shirt.

53
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,840
Sometimes we need some dynamic wrinkles effect, so we can use the

54
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:36,840
Scenic Comparison function.

55
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:46,840
First, open a position with a larger range of motion.

56
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:54,840
Following the change of the action position, there will be some more characteristic wrinkles in the pants.

57
00:05:54,840 --> 00:06:00,840
At this time, we choose the Scenic Comparison function, which will keep some of the wrinkle texture.

58
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:10,840
When you change the position to a vertical position, you can see that the Scenic Comparison version will keep some of the wrinkles.

59
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:18,840
This method is suitable for the effect of keeping some dynamic wrinkles on the static model.

60
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:24,840
After canceling the Scenic Comparison and simulation, the clothing will gradually return to its original state.

61
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:30,840
During the process, if you pause the simulation by pressing the control button, you can keep a foldable shape effect.

